  {
   "day": 23,
   "line": "👂 Overheard — Nadia (to Katarina): \"Betty's story has a fresh coat of paint.\" Nadia taps the table. \"Scrape it off and you get a Baker. Just don't scrape it in front of them.\""
  },
  {
   "day": 24,
   "line": "✨ Ability gained: Fusion Reactor (L1). The System installs your fusion pellet — properly, inside you. You never need to eat again: the pellet covers your metabolism, and your strikes and abilities burn with a steady reactor fire (1.25x, always on). One reactor per world, and it never comes out: not unslotted, not un-taught, not surrendered. Death is the only uninstall. But the hunger is gone, and "
  },
  {
   "day": 25,
   "line": "The village feels it before they understand it: Haven isn't just Haven anymore. Betty speaks at Emberhold's table now — earned, not appointed. And the other fire is watching what Haven does FIRST."
  },
  {
   "day": 27,
   "line": "The village feels it before they understand it: Haven isn't just Haven anymore. Betty speaks at Stonebridge's table now — earned, not appointed. And the other fire is watching what Haven does FIRST."
  },
  {
   "day": 28,
   "line": "The village feels it before they understand it: Haven isn't just Haven anymore. Betty speaks at Thornfield's table now — earned, not appointed. And the other fire is watching what Haven does FIRST."
  },
  {
   "day": 30,
   "line": "💔 A faction of Emberhold has turned cannibal — and split. The eaters walked. The Red Table is a new fire in the world now — 2 people under Rafael."
  },
  {
   "day": 30,
   "line": "📓 Codex: Emberhold split (cannibal). The Red Table formed; 2 petition at Haven's fire."
  },
  {
   "day": 31,
   "line": "You see smoke on the horizon. The Red Table — 2 people, 31 days in. fishing folk, by the look of it. They know 4 plants — 3 new to you. They've been here the whole time."
  },
  {
   "day": 31,
   "line": "🧳 A traveler says Emberhold burned — the whole fire, gone. (Wrong. It split: the eaters walked. The Red Table is the new fire.)"
  },
  {
   "day": 31,
   "line": "Fresh-cut stems on the southwest ground — someone else is working turf your crews use. (The Red Table's foragers, most likely. You walk the ground yourself: it's thinner than your crews alone could strip it.)"
  },
  {
   "day": 32,
   "line": "The southwest ground is thinning faster than your crews alone could strip it. The Red Table isn't slowing down — their foragers are on your turf most days now. Their speaker would probably want words. (Talk about the shared ground at their fire.)"
  },
  {
   "day": 33,
   "line": "Word later: they walked to The Red Table. Another fire in the world, whether you wanted it or not."
  },
  {
   "day": 33,
   "line": "The Red Table's speaker sent a runner: the southwest ground feeds both villages or neither. They want to talk — properly, at their fire. Ignoring this is also an answer."
  },
  {
   "day": 33,
   "line": "A runner from The Red Table, dusty and direct: \"Your foragers are stripping our side of the southwest ground. Back off — or we'll talk with teeth.\" (Trust -3. The commons cuts both ways.)"
  },
  {
   "day": 47,
   "line": "🧳 Word of Haven’s the televised games, new bindings is doing work out there — Word comes late, through traders: Emberhold and The Red Table have bound together — Emberhold primary. Other fires are climbing, too."
  },
  {
   "day": 47,
   "line": "📓 Codex: Emberhold and The Red Table bound; Emberhold primary."
  },
  {
   "day": 48,
   "line": "◈ WORD TRAVELS — riders from The Red Table bring talk of Haven. Out there they call you the Feared. The show's narration lingers on your hands."
