   "line": "🌙 Raid — The Red Table came in the night from the southwest. They carried off ~800 kcal from the pantry. Nobody's dead, but the message is clear: the ground is theirs too, and they're done asking. (Trust -10.)"
  },
  {
   "day": 142,
   "line": "🪞 You wake up somebody else. Olivia Elkington, 60 — a taxi driver. Their hands know different work now: Pyrokinesis, Dowsing, Echo Location, Green Whisper, Loud Chewer, Harvest Table."
  },
  {
   "day": 143,
   "line": "The table is being set — a lesser seat, priced for what you built. They are watching to see who comes to it."
  },
  {
   "day": 144,
   "line": "◈ WORD TRAVELS — riders from The Red Table bring talk of Haven. Out there they call you the Feared. The show's narration lingers on your hands."
  },
  {
   "day": 144,
   "line": "◈ THE TABLE — it is not a table. It's a ring of pale light, and around it, things with too many angles to be faces. Above it all — the audience. Trillions of eyes, and every one of them knows your name. The System speaks, and for once it isn't performing: \"HUMANITY PRESENTS ITS CASE.\""
  },
  {
   "day": 144,
   "line": "◈ THE AUDIT — the System reads your run back to you, and the galaxy listens. A lesser seat — national standing, waves 1–3 faced (16/9/3), with 1 wave-4 fought, 15 contests survived, 4 crises weathered. The table does not rise. It prices."
  },
  {
   "day": 144,
   "line": "The table notes 1 ascension from one village — its terms improve accordingly. Nobody has ever seen that before."
  },
  {
   "day": 144,
   "line": "◈ ABILITY — War-table: You read the table's fear the way you read weather. The Nielsen flinches first — you saw it."
  },
  {
   "day": 144,
   "line": "◈ THE FEARED — \"Look what eating built.\" The footage plays unasked — the deer, the fire, the ones who came for you and didn't come back. Nobody at the table is comfortable. That is the point."
  },
  {
   "day": 144,
   "line": "The table has read your ledger. The protected outnumber the killed; the food truth was shared. The light road is open."
  },
  {
   "day": 144,
   "line": "The deer. The cleanest kill. The table goes very still. Behind you, your own people go still too — a different stillness."
  },
  {
   "day": 144,
   "line": "You let them see it. All of it. The table recalculates. The fire back home burns a little lower."
  },
  {
   "day": 144,
   "line": "You spend it — the shield, not the sword. The small envoy stares. Your people stand a little straighter. Protective terror: the table writes it down and doesn't understand it, which is the point."
  },
  {
   "day": 144,
   "line": "The most frightening thing you ever did. The table doesn't know what to do with mercy from a predator. Neither do you, quite. But the audience weeps, and the galaxy learns that the feared one chose gentleness — and that choice echoes longer than any threat. The terror stays, pledged now: a shield over every village, forever."
  },
  {
   "day": 144,
   "line": "The terms held — the table had priced the village, ascension and all, and the village paid in full."
  },
  {
   "day": 144,
   "line": "You won. Say it plainly: you won. The village endures. The table signed. The galaxy applauds, and the applause is real, and you earned it."
